<title>UK: UK M4 grows provisional 9.4 pct in year to August.</title>
<headline>UK M4 grows provisional 9.4 pct in year to August.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England published the</p>
<p>following data on UK monetary aggregates for August -</p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY				   AUGUST	 JULY*</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (adjusted)	     +0.9	  +0.5</p>
<p>	  in year to date (adjusted)	    +9.4	  +9.0</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (unadjusted)	   +0.7	  unch</p>
<p>	  in year to date (unadjusted)	  +9.3	  +8.9</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks, building</p>
<p>     societies in billions of stg		4.8	   5.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecasts M4 +9.0 pct yr/yr, M4 lending</p>
<p>+5.4 billion stg. * Previously published final figures for July</p>
<p>    Three-month annual M4 rate (adj)	  +8.4	    n/a</p>
<p>    Six-month annual M4 rate   (adj)	  +9.4	    n/a</p>
<p>-- LONDON NEWSROOM ++44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
